<title>USA: TABLE - Amphenol Q2 oper shr increases.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Amphenol Q2 oper shr increases.</headline>
<dateline>WALLINGFORD, Conn. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.50		    $0.37</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.09		    $0.37</p>
<p> Oper income	     15,744		   17,408</p>
<p> Net			  2,929		   17,408</p>
<p> Revs		     226,996		  198,921</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  31,867		   47,328</p>
<p>	   6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Oper shr		   $0.87		    $0.73</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.53		    $0.73</p>
<p> Oper income	     33,271		   34,348</p>
<p> Net			 20,426		   34,348</p>
<p> Revs		     438,769		  393,743</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  38,258		   47,324</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE:  Net income for the second quarter of 1997 included an extraordinary loss for the early extinguishment of debt, net of tax, of $12,845,000, or $0.41 per share.</p>
<p>Net income for the first six months of 1997 included an extraordinary loss for the early extinguishment of debt, net of tax, of $12,845,000, or $0.34 per share.</p>
<p>The company said it completed a merger with an affiliate of Kohlberg Kravis Roberts &amp; Co whereby it incurred additional indebtednessand reduced its shares outstanding from approximately 44.7 million to 17.5 million.</p>
<p>Amphenol Corp.</p>
</text>
